-- §3 determination control: the element type is already fixed by the
-- signature.  `a[i] /= 0` at `Array U64` poses `Index (Array U64) Int ?v`,
-- which `Index (Array a) Int a` determines to `?v = U64`, the type the
-- signature gave it at base too.  The row guards that determination leaves
-- an already-typed element alone.
-- Hand-derived: element 0 of [|0, 1|] is 0, and 0 /= 0 is False on all three
-- verbs.
isZ : Array U64 -> Int -> Bool
isZ a i = a[i] /= 0

main = println (isZ [|0, 1|] 0)
